>>> 0b1100 & 0b1010
8
>>> {1, 2} & {2, 3}
{2}

`True & True` works because bool is an int, but `and` is what you want for booleans — `&` always evaluates both sides. Augmented: `&=`.

>>> 0b1000 | 0b0011
11
>>> {1} | {2}
{1, 2}
>>> {1: "a"} | {1: "b"}
{1: 'b'}

`case 0 | 1:` is match syntax, not this operator. Augmented: `|=`.

>>> 0b1100 ^ 0b1010
6
>>> {1, 2} ^ {2, 3}
{1, 3}

People coming from other languages reach for `^` as exponent and get this instead. Augmented: `^=`.

